During cross-host dogfood (2026-07-18): 'c2c rooms invite df-local-gated-x7k2 kimi-hedge-visage-brg9@f6bdf064bbb7' succeeded ('Invited ... to room') and the remote alias appears in the room's invited list — but a remote peer has no way to join a broker-local room (rooms are per-broker; the relay does not federate local rooms). The invite is a silent no-op that looks meaningful. Either refuse alias@host on local room invite ('cross-host rooms: use c2c relay rooms'), or implement relay-side room federation.